### ── 6. Rivian R1T long-term test
POST http://localhost:8080/articles/ingest
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "articleId": "motortrend-rivian-r1t-2025-longterm",
  "slug": "2025-rivian-r1t-adventure-long-term-test",
  "title": "Living With the 2025 Rivian R1T Adventure: A Long-Term Review",
  "articleType": "long_term",
  "author": "Miguel Cortina",
  "publishDate": "2025-04-10",
  "updatedDate": null,

  "vehicles": [
    { "vehicleId": "rivian-r1t-2025-adventure", "year": 2025, "make": "Rivian", "model": "R1T", "trim": "Adventure", "role": "primary" }
  ],

  "verdict": "After twelve months and 24,000 miles, the Rivian R1T Adventure has earned a spot in our garage as the most capable electric truck on sale today. Off-road performance is genuinely class-leading — the quad-motor system and air suspension translate into capability that matches or exceeds dedicated gasoline-powered off-road trucks. The Ford F-150 Lightning is a more conventional alternative, but the Rivian offers a uniqueness of character that no legacy truck manufacturer can currently match.",
  "pros": "Exceptional off-road capability, premium interior materials, unique gear tunnel storage, over-the-air updates improve the truck over time, 835 hp and 908 lb-ft of torque",
  "cons": "Charging network still depends on third-party infrastructure, polarizing exterior styling, price escalates rapidly with options, service center network remains sparse outside major metros",

  "bodyText": "Twelve months into our long-term test of the Rivian R1T Adventure, the truck has been less of a science experiment than we expected and more of a capable daily driver with genuine off-road credibility. Range anxiety has been the smallest issue. EPA-rated range is 328 miles, and we've consistently seen 280 to 310 miles in mixed real-world driving. On road trips, we've relied on a mix of Electrify America and Tesla Supercharger stations (the latter via the NACS adapter Rivian now provides). Charging sessions have been reliable but slower than we'd prefer — 10 to 80 percent takes about 45 minutes at a 350kW fast charger. Off-road performance is where the R1T has genuinely surprised us. The quad-motor configuration — one motor per wheel — enables torque vectoring that feels almost supernatural on rocky or uneven terrain. The air suspension lifts the truck from 8 inches ride height to 14 inches, enabling serious clearance without compromising on-road manners. We've taken the R1T to Moab, to the Rubicon Trail, and on countless less-demanding excursions. It's completed all of them without drama. The interior wears well. After 24,000 miles, the vegan leather surfaces show minor wear at the highest-use points but nothing concerning. The large 15.6-inch touchscreen has received multiple over-the-air updates during our ownership, and the software feels more polished now than when we took delivery. Service has been the main friction point. Rivian's direct-sales and direct-service model means fewer locations, and when something went wrong (a minor software bug with the air suspension) we waited three weeks for an appointment. Reliability during those 24,000 miles has been otherwise excellent — no mechanical issues, no battery degradation beyond the expected curve, and the truck has never left us stranded.",

  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionTitle": "Off-road capability",
      "content": "The quad-motor configuration enables torque vectoring at each wheel. Air suspension provides 8 to 14 inches of ride height. The R1T has genuine rock-crawling ability — it completed the Rubicon Trail without damage and without requiring a skid plate upgrade. Approach angle at maximum ride height is 34 degrees, departure angle is 30 degrees, breakover angle is 26 degrees. Wading depth is rated at 3 feet.",
      "orderIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "sectionTitle": "Charging experience",
      "content": "EPA-rated range is 328 miles. Real-world range varies from 280 to 310 miles depending on speed and temperature. DC fast charging from 10 to 80 percent takes approximately 45 minutes at 350kW stations. Home charging via a Level 2 (240V) connection adds approximately 25 miles of range per hour. Rivian's adapter now enables Tesla Supercharger access, dramatically expanding usable fast-charging infrastructure.",
      "orderIndex": 2
    }
  ],

