  "verdict": "Over a five-year ownership window at 15,000 miles annually, the Tesla Model 3 Long Range saves approximately $4,200 in running costs versus the Toyota Camry Hybrid. However, the Tesla costs approximately $14,000 more to purchase. The crossover point where the Tesla becomes cheaper to own is roughly year nine for the average driver. For drivers exceeding 20,000 annual miles, the crossover point moves to year six.",
  "pros": "EV: lowest per-mile running cost, no oil changes, instant torque, home charging convenience. Hybrid: lower upfront cost, no charging anxiety, existing fuel infrastructure, lower insurance premiums",
